raw:
- The Court must be guided by what, consistent with the law applicable to the minor, appears to be for the welfare of the minor — **Guardians and Wards Act 1890, s. 17(1)**.  
- In determining the welfare of the minor, the Court shall have regard to the **age, sex and religion** of the minor — **Guardians and Wards Act 1890, s. 17(2)**.  
- The Court must also consider ancillary factors such as:  
  - The **near relations** of the minor and their place of residence;  
  - Whether a guardian of the person or property (or both) has already been appointed by a person entitled to do so;  
  - Whether any application has previously been made to any Court regarding the guardianship of the minor — **Guardians and Wards Act 1890, s. 10(f) & (g)**.

